# 📌 6. What is an Iterator?

An iterator is an object that keeps track of its current position while going through an iterable.

Example:

```python
numbers = [10, 20, 30]

iterator = iter(numbers)
```

Now:

```text
numbers
   ↓
[10, 20, 30]

   ↓ iter()

iterator
   ↓
10 → 20 → 30
```

The iterator remembers where it currently is.

