# 🔐 51. Cybersecurity Connection

Iterators are useful because cybersecurity systems frequently deal with **large amounts of data**.

Examples:

```text
Firewall logs
Authentication logs
Web server logs
Network events
PCAP-related processing
Security alerts
CSV datasets
Threat intelligence feeds
System events
```

Instead of thinking:

```text
"Load everything and then process it."
```

you can often think:

```text
"Read one item → process it → move to the next item."
```

For example:

```text
10 GB log file
      ↓
Read one line
      ↓
Check for suspicious activity
      ↓
Read next line
      ↓
Check again
      ↓
Continue...
```

This is a very useful concept for cybersecurity automation.

