# 🏆 DAY 14 COMPLETE

**Python Topic:** Iterators
**Learning Platform:** W3Schools
**Status:** ✅ Completed

### Key Takeaway:

> **An iterable is something you can loop over, while an iterator is the object that remembers where you are and provides the next item one at a time.**

The most important functions and methods are:

```python
iter()
next()
__iter__()
__next__()
```

And when there are no more values:

```python
StopIteration
```

### Mental Model

```text
             ITERABLE
                 │
                 │ iter()
                 ▼
             ITERATOR
                 │
                 │ next()
                 ▼
              ITEM 1
                 │
                 │ next()
                 ▼
              ITEM 2
                 │
                 │ next()
                 ▼
              ITEM 3
                 │
                 ▼
          No items remaining
                 │
                 ▼
          StopIteration
```

